Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-08-2001||03:57 PM||||Way back when I was in the coast guard someone had tossed an FM/8track in the trash can.<BR> <BR>  I looked at it, hooked it up to a spare battery, and it took me about 20 seconds to figure out the power switch had failed.<P>  so I put a new switch on the side of it that I had laying around, and installed it in my sisters bug, which only had the stock AM radio. screwed it to the underside of the dash board, and put a nice pair of jensen triaxial 6 x 9s behind the back seat (had those left over from another car.<P>   about a year later someone broke into her car and stole the FM/8track player.<P>   they left the hidden speakers<P>   and they also left behind a craftsman screwdriver and a nice pair of vicegrips on the floor of the car.<P>   Since the deck was free, and since I still have the tools (20 years later!) - i figure I made out on the 'transaction'<P>  before I stick any non-stock radio in a car I always pause and wonder if the improvement in audio quality will be worth the risk of someone trashing the car and the dashboard to steal it.<P> and now that I think of it, I havent put an aftermarket audio system in any of my cars since, ok since 1984, when I bought a new rabbit that had no radio at all.<P>  usually for long trips most people bring a portable CD player w/headphones anyway.<P>   Im thinking of trying out one of those portable CD players that play through your FM radio - you set the radio to 88.0 and it picks up the music from the CD. It can be up to 20 feet from the antenna - I think they are about $40 at BJs or Samsclub.<P>  If I get one Ill let you all know how it works.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||06-08-2001||04:17 PM||||what we really need is an audio system that is completely hidden in the car - cant see the speakers, the amp and receiver are in the trunk somewhere, and it all works on a remote you keep in your pocket, or toss in the glove compartment.<P>  so if someone looks in the car they see nothing but the stock radio in the dashboard.||||reg||1
Z||000013||saleenfiero||06-08-2001||04:37 PM||||You can get those kind of stereos that looks like original decks.  I seen them for older classics like stock Corvettes and stuff.  They use them to keep the original look with some good sound options too.||||reg||1
