Z||000018||fyerstarter||06-13-2001||10:46 PM||||Haha don't think because you live in a nice neighborhood you are safe from theives. That is a common misconception. Think about it, if you are a crook do you want to break into some ****ed up ghetto ride parked down by the 7-11 in your own hood and get off with a $25 swapmeet stereo or do you wanna take a trip up to where the rich people live and come home with the good **** ? <P>That being said sorry to hear bout your stereo. I had $1500 worth of stereo equipment stolen out of my eclipse a few years back. That's what I get though for bumpin my ****  in and out of the parking lot every day. Someones is bound to notice sometime and relieve you of your stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Jake_Dragon||06-14-2001||07:30 AM||||Is it the thief or JVC I should look out for?<BR>I agree why would anyone steal from a poor neighborhood? Because no one is looking. The car next door had $1000 worth of damage, my car only had $70 why? The lights came on and scared the crapp out of them. Wish I had my web cam on that! Big Brother is watch let them come back.||||reg||1
